No violations in 4 packages.

  Checked: the layer rule, the handler/transport rule and the handler/driver
  rule — each directly and through a helper package.

  NOT checked: the cross-module rule. It compares feature modules, which it
  finds by a `modules` path segment — internal/modules/<feature>/… , the tree
  `warren new` generates — and this project has none, so nothing was compared
  across features.

  NOT checked: _test.go files. A test importing its own feature's
  infrastructure is how a test is written, so the walk skips them — which
  also means a test file is the one place these rules do not reach.

  Carve-out: a feature's module.go MAY import a sibling feature. That is
  where a module value is wired, so the cross-module rule exempts that one
  filename and no other.
